# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sardar CRM environment variables
# Copy to .env.local for local dev, or set in your host's
# project settings (e.g. Vercel) for deployment.
#
# NOTE: If these Supabase vars are ABSENT or still placeholders, the
# app automatically runs in demo mode with the full seeded data (see README).
# Placeholder values like "your-project.supabase.co" / "your-anon-key" are
# treated as unset so a copied .env.example cannot silently "look live".
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Supabase (Postgres + Auth + Storage + Realtime)
# Uncomment and fill in with your real Supabase credentials.
# When these are absent, the app automatically runs in demo mode.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxxxxxx.supabase.co
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...

# Required ONLY for agency user management (creating employee logins from
# Settings -> Team access). Find it in Supabase Dashboard -> Project Settings
# -> API -> service_role (secret). NEVER expose this in the browser.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key

# Required for storing project credential passwords (WP admin, cPanel, FTP, ...)
# ENCRYPTED at rest (AES-256-GCM). Any non-empty string works; it is hashed to
# a 32-byte key. Set a long, random, STABLE value — changing it makes already-
# saved passwords unrecoverable.
# Without this var: Supabase mode FAILS CLOSED (saving/revealing credentials
# errors out); demo mode stores passwords as-is.
# CREDENTIALS_ENCRYPTION_KEY=generate-a-long-random-string

# Optional — real AI proposal generation (otherwise a smart template is used)
# USER_LLM_API_KEY=your-llm-key
# USER_LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# USER_LLM_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
